Prepare indices at stratum boundaries

Compile each stratum's input indices and transitive native transport
dependencies before Rust generation. Prepare the selected indices before
evaluation and pass direct references to rules. Keep simultaneous
scheduling as the default, with one preparation plan per round.

Refresh only the member relations needed by the stratum, including graph
and application dependencies for nested models. Propagate secondary
orders from owned tuples so inherited subtrees remain shared. Refresh
all public views on return and before close_until callbacks.

Retain source snapshots and catch up secondary indices with borrowed,
sharing-aware differences. Share unchanged snapshots and derived indices
between consumers. Public queries outside evaluation remain lazy.

Cover index selection, late graph edges, cycles, inherited subtree
sharing, equality replacements, and both scheduling modes. Leave
canonicalization-aware branch updates for separate work.
